cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use hpoadj, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "hpoadj: cohort augmentation and leave-one-publication-out for HPO annotation files"
version: 0.0.2
date-released: 2026-11-08
license: Apache-2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24054540
repository-code: "https://github.com/P2GX/hpoadj"
url: "https://github.com/P2GX/hpoadj"
abstract: >-
  Adjusts HPO annotation files (phenotype.hpoa) for phenopacket-based benchmarking of
  phenotype-driven diagnostic tools: adds the disease annotations implied by a curated
  phenopacket cohort and removes, per publication, that publication's contribution so that
  no individual contributes to the disease profile it is scored against.
authors:
  - family-names: Graefe
    given-names: Adam
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-8124-8864"
    affiliation: "Berlin Institute of Health at Charité, Universitätsmedizin Berlin"
keywords:
  - Human Phenotype Ontology
  - GA4GH Phenopackets
  - benchmarking
  - rare disease
  - LIRICAL
